## 3. Source Code Added or Modified

### Files added

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `kernel/debug.h` | Part A. Category bits, level constants, the `dprintf` macro, the `DBGCTL_*` operation codes, and the shared `DBG_CATNAMES` / `DBG_LEVELNAMES` name tables. |
| `kernel/debug.c` | Part A. The `debug_mask` and `debug_level` globals and the two prefix helpers, `dbg_catname()` and `dbg_pidstr()`. |
| `user/dbg.c` | Part C. The user-space tool that reads and modifies the mask and level. |
| `tools/drive.py` | Test harness used to capture some transcripts non-interactively. Not part of the kernel or the build. |

### Files modified

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `Makefile` | Added `$K/debug.o` to `OBJS`, `$U/_dbg` to `UPROGS`, and the `DEBUG ?= 1` / `-DDEBUG` build switch. |
| `kernel/syscall.h` | Allocated `SYS_debugctl 23`. |
| `kernel/syscall.c` | Added the `sys_debugctl` extern and its entry in the `syscalls[]` table. |
| `kernel/sysproc.c` | Part B. Implemented `sys_debugctl()`. |
| `kernel/proc.c` | Part D. `dprintf` calls in `allocproc`, `freeproc`, `userinit`, `kfork`, `kexit`, `kwait`, `kkill`, and `scheduler`. Changed `reparent()` from `void` to `int` so it returns the number of children reparented. |
| `kernel/exec.c` | Part D. `dprintf` calls in `kexec` for the success path, the not-found path, and the `bad:` error path. |
| `user/user.h` | Added the `debugctl()` prototype. |
| `user/usys.pl` | Added `entry("debugctl")` so the syscall stub is generated. |

The tree builds cleanly with `-Wall -Werror` both at `make` and at `make DEBUG=0`.

